I will point out **what each piece does**, **why it is written that way**, and give a short **high‑level picture** of the whole algorithm.  
The code is a typical “producer‑workers‑consumer” pipeline that

1. reads FASTQ records (DNA sequencing reads) from a file,  
2. maps each read to a *pseudo‑alignment* index, and  
3. streams the mapping results to a single consumer that prints progress (and later would write them to disk).

