* Each *.db* file contains one word per line (empty lines are ignored).
* The *text* file may contain several lines; the program treats every line
  independently, substitutes all placeholders and writes the **last**
  processed line to the output file (the task description mentions a single
  line, but the code works with many as well).  
  If you need all processed lines, simply move the `fprintf` call inside the
  loop that reads the text file.
* Randomness is seeded by `srand(time(NULL))` (placed at the beginning of
  `main` if you prefer deterministic output – remove or set a fixed seed).

