|---------|----------------|
| `dma_alloc_coherent()` | Gives a physically contiguous buffer that is automatically mapped for DMA (no `dma_map_single` required). |
| `dma_cap_zero()/dma_cap_set()` + `dma_request_chan_by_mask()` | Pulls a DMA channel that advertises `DMA_MEMCPY`.  On many SoCs the *internal* DMA engine (e.g., PL330 on ARM, DWC‑DMA on many Qualcomm platforms) fulfills this. |
