| `CONFIG_STAGING_MEDIA` (optional) | Some platforms expose a *dummy* memcpy DMA channel in the `staging` tree. Not needed for the test but may be useful. | No |

You can verify these are set by looking at `/boot/config-$(uname -r)` or running `make menuconfig` in your kernel source.

> **Tip:** On a typical x86 workstation the kernel ships with `CONFIG_DMA_VIRTUAL_CHANNELS=y`. The test will therefore succeed even without any “real” DMA controller, because the virtual engine just copies memory using the CPU but still goes through the DMA‑engine API. On an ARM SoC you will usually see a hardware‑backed channel (e.g., `pl330`, `dwc_dma`, `gdma`, etc.) and you’ll get a genuine DMA transfer.

