The current `player` struct only stores a pointer to the current room.  
We need a place to keep the items that the player discovers:

```c
#define MAX_INVENTORY  20          // arbitrary limit

typedef struct player {
    room *currentRoom;
    char *inventory[MAX_INVENTORY];
    int  inventoryCount;
} player;
```

*Add the two new fields (`inventory` and `inventoryCount`) to the definition of `player`.*  
No other part of the code needs to be changed – the `createPlayer()` function will initialise `inventoryCount` to 0 (see step 4).

