## 3. Write the function that implements the new action  

```c
/* -------------------------------------------------------------
   Search the current room for a hidden item.
   Returns true if an item was found, false otherwise.
   ------------------------------------------------------------- */
static bool searchCurrentRoom(player *p)
{
    /* 30 % chance to find something – feel free to tweak */
    if (rand() % 100 < 30) {
        /* a tiny pool of possible treasure strings */
        const char *possible[] = {
            "a glittering gemstone",
            "an ancient coin",
            "a rusted key",
            "a mysterious scroll"
        };
        const char *found = possible[rand() % (sizeof possible / sizeof possible[0])];

        /* store it in the inventory (if we have space) */
        if (p->inventoryCount < MAX_INVENTORY) {
            p->inventory[p->inventoryCount] = malloc(strlen(found) + 1);
            strcpy(p->inventory[p->inventoryCount], found);
            p->inventoryCount++;
            printf("You search the room… and find %s!\n", found);
        } else {
            printf("You find %s, but your bag is already full.\n", found);
        }
        return true;
    } else {
        printf("You search the room but find nothing of interest.\n");
        return false;
    }
}
```

*Key points*

* `rand()` is already seeded in `loadRooms()`, so we can reuse it.
* The function updates the player’s inventory and informs the player.
