## 1️⃣ Java Networking – The Foundations

| Concept | Core API | Typical Use‑Case | Quick Example |
|---------|----------|------------------|----------------|
| **IP addressing & DNS** | `java.net.InetAddress` | Resolve host names, test reachability | `InetAddress a = InetAddress.getByName("example.com");` |
| **TCP sockets** (reliable, ordered) | `java.net.Socket` / `java.net.ServerSocket` | Custom binary protocols, chat, FTP, SMTP, etc. | See **Section 1.2** |
| **UDP datagrams** (unreliable, connection‑less) | `java.net.DatagramSocket` / `java.net.DatagramPacket` | DNS queries, VoIP, gaming, syslog | See **Section 1.3** |
| **URL/URI handling** | `java.net.URL`, `java.net.URI` | Fetching resources, parsing query strings | `new URL("https://api.github.com");` |
| **HTTP/HTTPS client (blocking)** | `java.net.HttpURLConnection` (pre‑Java 11) | Simple GET/POST, basic auth | `HttpURLConnection con = (HttpURLConnection)url.openConnection();` |
| **HTTP/HTTPS client (modern, async)** | `java.net.http.HttpClient` (Java 11+) | HTTP/2, async, reactive streams | See **Section 1.5** |
| **NIO (non‑blocking I/O)** | `java.nio.channels.SocketChannel`, `ServerSocketChannel`, `Selector` | High‑throughput servers, multiplexed I/O | See **Section 1.6** |
| **Reactive / Netty‑based** | Project Reactor, Vert.x, Netty, Undertow | Event‑loop, back‑pressure, micro‑services | Mentioned in **Section 1.7** |

> **Why it matters:** Most web‑service frameworks (JAX‑WS, JAX‑RS, Spring MVC/Boot) sit on top of these primitives. Understanding them helps you troubleshoot latency, TLS handshake failures, or design a custom protocol when needed.

