## 3️⃣ Loading the Certificate & Private Key  

The RN‑FTP spec requires **SHA‑256‑with‑RSA** signature. Below is a reusable helper:

```java
package com.mycompany.fiskal.util;

import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.security.*;
import java.security.cert.CertificateException;
import java.security.cert.X509Certificate;
import java.util.Enumeration;
import javax.net.ssl.*;

public final class KeystoreUtil {

    private KeystoreUtil() {}

    /** Loads a PKCS#12 keystore and returns the private key + cert chain */
    public static KeyAndCert loadKeyAndCert(String pkcs12Path, char[] password)
            throws KeyStoreException, NoSuchAlgorithmException,
                   CertificateException, UnrecoverableKeyException, IOException {

        KeyStore ks = KeyStore.getInstance("PKCS12");
        try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(pkcs12Path)) {
            ks.load(fis, password);
        }

        // Usually the keystore contains exactly one entry
        Enumeration<String> aliases = ks.aliases();
        if (!aliases.hasMoreElements()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Keystore is empty");
        }
        String alias = aliases.nextElement();
        PrivateKey pk = (PrivateKey) ks.getKey(alias, password);
        X509Certificate cert = (X509Certificate) ks.getCertificate(alias);
        return new KeyAndCert(pk, cert);
    }

    /** Simple holder */
    public static final class KeyAndCert {
        public final PrivateKey privateKey;
        public final X509Certificate certificate;

        public KeyAndCert(PrivateKey pk, X509Certificate cert) {
            this.privateKey = pk;
            this.certificate = cert;
        }
    }

    /** Creates an SSLContext that trusts the default JDK roots (still needed for HTTPS). */
    public static SSLContext defaultSslContext() throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, KeyManagementException {
        SSLContext ctx = SSLContext.getInstance("TLS");
        ctx.init(null, null, null);
        return ctx;
    }
}
```

**Usage**

```java
final String keystorePath = "/opt/fiskal/cert.p12";
final char[] keystorePwd = "secret".toCharArray();

KeystoreUtil.KeyAndCert kac = KeystoreUtil.loadKeyAndCert(keystorePath, keystorePwd);
PrivateKey privateKey = kac.privateKey;
X509Certificate cert = kac.certificate;
```

> **Tip:** Keep the keystore password out of source code – use environment variables, JCEKS, or a secret‑manager (Vault, Azure Key Vault, …).

