## 5️⃣ Digital Signature  

### 5.1 XML‑DSig (for the XML endpoint)

```java
package com.mycompany.fiskal.sign;

import org.apache.xml.security.Init;
import org.apache.xml.security.signature.XMLSignature;
import org.apache.xml.security.transforms.Transforms;
import org.apache.xml.security.utils.Constants;
import org.w3c.dom.*;

import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import java.security.PrivateKey;
import java.security.cert.X509Certificate;

public final class XmlSigner {

    static {
        // Initialise Apache Santuario once
        Init.init();
    }

    private XmlSigner() {}

    /**
     * Signs the given XML Document (the whole document) and adds a <Signature> element
     * under its root as required by RN‑FTP.
     */
    public static Document sign(Document doc, PrivateKey privateKey, X509Certificate cert)
            throws Exception {

        // 1️⃣ Create Signature object (enveloped signature)
        XMLSignature sig = new XMLSignature(doc, "", XMLSignature.ALGO_ID_SIGNATURE_RSA_SHA256);

        // 2️⃣ Insert <Signature> as the first child of the root element
        Element root = doc.getDocumentElement();
        root.insertBefore(sig.getElement(), root.getFirstChild());

        // 3️⃣ Add the transforms – enveloped + canonicalisation (exc. comments)
        Transforms transforms = new Transforms(doc);
        transforms.addTransform(Transforms.TRANSFORM_ENVELOPED_SIGNATURE);
        transforms.addTransform(Transforms.TRANSFORM_C14N_EXCL_OMIT_COMMENTS);
        sig.addDocument("", transforms, Constants.ALGO_ID_DIGEST_SHA256);

        // 4️⃣ Attach the signing certificate (optional but recommended)
        sig.addKeyInfo(cert);

        // 5️⃣ Compute the signature
        sig.sign(privateKey);

        return doc;
    }

    /** Helper: convert a Document to pretty‑printed XML string (for logging) */
    public static String toString(Document doc) throws Exception {
        java.io.StringWriter sw = new java.io.StringWriter();
        javax.xml.transform.Transformer transformer = 
            javax.xml.transform.TransformerFactory.newInstance().newTransformer();
        transformer.setOutputProperty(javax.xml.transform.OutputKeys.INDENT, "yes");
        transformer.transform(new javax.xml.transform.dom.DOMSource(doc),
                new javax.xml.transform.stream.StreamResult(sw));
        return sw.toString();
    }
}
```

**How to use**

```java
// 1️⃣ Marshal POJO → Document
Invoice invoice = buildInvoice(); // see later
JAXBContext ctx = JAXBContext.newInstance(Invoice.class);
Marshaller marshaller = ctx.createMarshaller();
marshaller.setProperty(Marshaller.JAXB_FORMATTED_OUTPUT, true);
DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
dbf.setNamespaceAware(true);
Document doc = dbf.newDocumentBuilder().newDocument();
marshaller.marshal(invoice, doc);

// 2️⃣ Sign
Document signedDoc = XmlSigner.sign(doc, privateKey, cert);
String xmlPayload = XmlSigner.toString(signedDoc);
```

### 5.2 JSON signature (if you use the JSON endpoint)

The specification asks for a **Base64‑encoded SHA‑256‑with‑RSA** signature over the **UTF‑8 bytes** of the JSON **without the `signature` field**. The usual approach:

```java
package com.mycompany.fiskal.sign;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.PrivateKey;
import java.security.Signature;
import java.util.Base64;

public final class JsonSigner {

    private static final ObjectMapper MAPPER = new ObjectMapper();

    private JsonSigner() {}

    /**
     * Computes a Base64 signature and returns a new JSON node with a "signature"
     * property set.
     *
     * @param documentWithoutSignature JSON representation of the document *without* the signature field
     * @param privateKey RSA private key
     */
    public static ObjectNode sign(ObjectNode documentWithoutSignature, PrivateKey privateKey) throws Exception {
        // 1️⃣ canonicalise: deterministic ordering of fields (Jackson does it if we serialise the node directly)
        String canonicalJson = MAPPER.writeValueAsString(documentWithoutSignature);

        // 2️⃣ Sign the UTF‑8 bytes
        Signature sig = Signature.getInstance("SHA256withRSA");
        sig.initSign(privateKey);
        sig.update(canonicalJson.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        byte[] rawSig = sig.sign();

        // 3️⃣ Base64‑encode
        String b64 = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(rawSig);

        // 4️⃣ put back the signature field
        ObjectNode signed = documentWithoutSignature.deepCopy();
        signed.put("signature", b64);
        return signed;
    }
}
```

**Usage**

```java
FiscalDocument doc = buildFiscalDocument(); // without setting signature
ObjectNode node = (ObjectNode) JsonSigner.MAPPER.valueToTree(doc);
ObjectNode signedNode = JsonSigner.sign(node, privateKey);
String jsonPayload = JsonSigner.MAPPER.writeValueAsString(signedNode);
```

