## 7️⃣ Handling the Response  

The response contains either:

* **Success** → a `<JIR>` element (XML) or `"jir"` property (JSON) and a **digital signature** of the response (optional validation).  
* **Error** → an `<Error>` block with **code** and **message**.

### 7.1 XML parsing

```java
import jakarta.xml.bind.*;

public class XmlResponseParser {

    @XmlRootElement(name = "Response")
    public static class Response {
        @XmlElement(name = "JIR")
        public String jir;

        @XmlElement(name = "Signature")
        public String signature; // Base64
    }

    public static Response parse(String xml) throws JAXBException {
        JAXBContext ctx = JAXBContext.newInstance(Response.class);
        Unmarshaller um = ctx.createUnmarshaller();
        return (Response) um.unmarshal(new java.io.StringReader(xml));
    }
}
```

