### 7.3 Verifying the response signature (optional but recommended)

The RN‑FTP server signs the response with its own certificate (available on the Fina website). You can verify it the same way you verify your own signature – using the public key from the supplied certificate.

```java
public static boolean verifyXmlSignature(Document doc, X509Certificate serverCert) throws Exception {
    NodeList nl = doc.getElementsByTagNameNS(XMLSignature.XMLNS, "Signature");
    if (nl.getLength() == 0) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("No Signature element found");
    }
    XMLSignature sig = new XMLSignature((Element) nl.item(0), null);
    return sig.checkSignatureValue(serverCert);
}
```

For JSON, just recompute the hash and verify with `Signature.getInstance("SHA256withRSA")` using the server’s public key.

