## 10️⃣ Testing – What to Verify Before Going Live  

| What to test | How |
|--------------|-----|
| **Schema compliance** | Use the XSD/JSON‑schema validator (e.g. `javax.xml.validation.SchemaFactory` for XML or `com.github.fge.jsonschema` for JSON). |
| **Signature correctness** | Verify with OpenSSL: `openssl dgst -sha256 -verify pubkey.pem -signature sig.bin payload.txt`. |
| **Endpoint connectivity** | Hit the **sandbox** environment (if you have one) or use the “test mode” flag (`"test": true` in JSON). |
| **Idempotency** | Send the same receipt twice – you should receive the same JIR. |
| **Error handling** | Force a failure (e.g. wrong OIB) and check that you receive a documented error code (`"ERR-101"` etc.). |
| **Performance** | Measure round‑trip time (< 2 seconds is typical). |
| **Persistence** | Simulate a DB crash and verify you can still recover unsent receipts from a dead‑letter queue. |

Most fiscal‑module vendors provide a **test certificate** that points to a sandbox server (`https://test.apis-it.hr`). Use that while developing.

