## 2. Data model – what we store for every file  

```java
package dev.example.fileindex;

import java.io.Serializable;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.Objects;

/**
 * A tiny, immutable DTO that represents the information we keep for a single file.
 * Feel free to extend it (e.g. store SHA‑256 hash, MIME‑type, …) – just keep it
 * serialisable (Jackson works with POJOs).
 */
public final class FileMeta implements Serializable {
    private final String path;          // absolute path, case‑preserving
    private final long size;            // in bytes
    private final long lastModified;    // epoch‑millis
    // we also keep a lower‑cased file name for quick case‑insensitive searches
    private final String nameLowerCase;

    public FileMeta(String path, long size, long lastModified) {
        this.path = Objects.requireNonNull(path);
        this.size = size;
        this.lastModified = lastModified;
        this.nameLowerCase = new java.io.File(path).getName().toLowerCase();
    }

    // Getters (Jackson needs them for serialization)
    public String getPath()          { return path; }
    public long   getSize()          { return size; }
    public long   getLastModified() { return lastModified; }
    public String getNameLowerCase(){ return nameLowerCase; }

    // Helper used by the search engine
    public boolean nameMatches(String queryLower) {
        return nameLowerCase.contains(queryLower);
    }

    @Override public String toString() {
        return String.format("FileMeta[path=%s, size=%d, modified=%s]",
                path, size, Instant.ofEpochMilli(lastModified));
    }
}
```

