## 6. Searching the index  

A simple, **case‑insensitive** substring search in the file name.  
If you need more complex queries (regex, size range, date range, …) modify `FileMetaSearcher`.

```java
package dev.example.fileindex;

import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentMap;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

/**
 * Provides a thin API over the in‑memory map.
 * The implementation is deliberately straightforward, but you can plug in
 * Lucene, Apache Tika, or any other engine if you want full‑text.
 */
public final class FileMetaSearcher {

    private final ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index;

    public FileMetaSearcher(ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index) {
        this.index = Objects.requireNonNull(index);
    }

    /** Returns up to {@code maxResults} file paths whose *file name* contains the query (case‑insensitive). */
    public List<FileMeta> searchByName(String query, int maxResults) {
        if (query == null || query.isBlank()) return List.of();
        String queryLC = query.toLowerCase();

        return index.values()
                .stream()
                .filter(meta -> meta.nameMatches(queryLC))
                .limit(maxResults)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
    }

    /** Returns the exact `FileMeta` for a given absolute path, or null if not present. */
    public FileMeta getExact(String absolutePath) {
        return index.get(absolutePath);
    }
}
```

