## 7. Watching the file‑system – keep the index up‑to‑date  

`WatchService` can register **only a single directory at a time**.  
To watch the whole drive we must register **every directory recursively** (and re‑register when a new directory appears).

A few gotchas & how we handle them:

| Issue | Why it matters | Our mitigation |
|-------|----------------|----------------|
| **OS limit on the number of watches** (e.g. Linux `inotify.max_user_watches`) | Registering *all* directories can exceed the limit on a large drive. | The example falls back to a **periodic rescanning** (every `RESCAN_INTERVAL_MS`) if the limit is hit. You can increase the kernel limit (`sudo sysctl -w fs.inotify.max_user_watches=524288`). |
| **Directory deleted while being watched** | `WatchKey` becomes invalid. | We simply cancel the key (`key.cancel()`) – the next periodic scan will purge stale entries. |
| **Overflow events** (`OVERFLOW`) | The OS could drop events when the queue fills up. | On overflow we trigger a **full rescan** of the affected root to guarantee consistency. |
| **Performance** | Registering millions of directories can be slow. | Registration is done **once per drive** on start‑up, in a separate thread, and uses the same `ConcurrentHashMap` as the index. |

```java
package dev.example.fileindex;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import static java.nio.file.StandardWatchEventKinds.*;

/**
 * Core class that watches *all* directories on all drives and updates the index.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   DriveWatcher watcher = new DriveWatcher(indexMap);
 *   watcher.start();                 // starts background threads
 *   ...
 *   watcher.stop();                  // graceful shutdown
 */
public final class DriveWatcher {

    private static final long RESCAN_INTERVAL_MS = TimeUnit.MINUTES.toMillis(30);
    private final ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index;

    // One WatchService per *root* (drive) – we cannot share one across different filesystems.
    private final List<WatchService> services = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();

    // Executor that runs the watch loops
    private final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();

    // Scheduler for periodic full rescans (in case something slipped through)
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();

    public DriveWatcher(ConcurrentMap<String, FileMeta> index) {
        this.index = Objects.requireNonNull(index);
    }

    /** Starts watching all current drives and schedules periodic rescans. */
    public void start() throws IOException {
        for (File root : DriveDetector.listRootDrives()) {
            registerRecursively(root.toPath());
        }
        // Periodic safety net
        scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(this::fullRescanAllDrives,
                RESCAN_INTERVAL_MS, RESCAN_INTERVAL_MS, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }

    /** Stops all background threads and closes the WatchServices. */
    public void stop() {
        // Shut down the periodic rescans
        scheduler.shutdownNow();
        // Stop the watch loops
        executor.shutdownNow();
        // Close every WatchService (throws IOException – ignore, we are shutting down)
        for (WatchService ws : services) {
            try { ws.close(); } catch (IOException ignored) {}
        }
    }

    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /*  1️⃣  Register every directory recursively under a given root           */
    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void registerRecursively(Path root) throws IOException {
        WatchService ws = FileSystems.getDefault().newWatchService();
        services.add(ws);

        // Walk the file tree *once* and register each directory.
        Files.walkFileTree(root, new SimpleFileVisitor<>() {
            @Override
            public FileVisitResult preVisitDirectory(Path dir, BasicFileAttributes attrs) {
                try {
                    dir.register(ws, ENTRY_CREATE, ENTRY_DELETE, ENTRY_MODIFY);
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    System.err.println("Cannot watch directory: " + dir + " (" + e.getMessage() + ")");
                    // Continue – some directories (e.g., system protected) may be unwatched.
                }
                return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
            }
        });

        // Start a background task that *processes* events for this watch service.
        executor.submit(() -> processEvents(ws, root));
    }

    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /*  2️⃣  The event‑processing loop for a single WatchService                */
    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void processEvents(WatchService ws, Path root) {
        while (true) {
            WatchKey key;
            try {
                // Wait indefinitely for an event (or interruption)
                key = ws.take();
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                break; // exit loop → thread ends
            } catch (ClosedWatchServiceException e) {
                break; // service closed → thread ends
            }

            Path watchedDir = (Path) key.watchable();

            for (WatchEvent<?> ev : key.pollEvents()) {
                WatchEvent.Kind<?> kind = ev.kind();

                // Overflow means we missed events → do a full rescan of the affected root.
                if (kind == OVERFLOW) {
                    System.err.println("Overflow detected – performing full rescan of " + root);
                    fullRescanRoot(root);
                    continue;
                }

                // Context is the *relative* path (relative to watchedDir)
                WatchEvent<Path> evPath = cast(ev);
                Path name = evPath.context();
                Path child = watchedDir.resolve(name);

                // -------------------------------------------------------------
                //   Handle CREATE / DELETE / MODIFY
                // -------------------------------------------------------------
                if (kind == ENTRY_CREATE) {
                    handleCreate(child);
                } else if (kind == ENTRY_DELETE) {
                    handleDelete(child);
                } else if (kind == ENTRY_MODIFY) {
                    handleModify(child);
                }
            }

            boolean valid = key.reset();
            if (!valid) {
                // The directory is no longer accessible – stop watching it.
                System.err.println("WatchKey no longer valid for " + watchedDir);
            }
        }
    }

    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    private static <T> WatchEvent<T> cast(WatchEvent<?> ev) {
        return (WatchEvent<T>) ev;
    }

    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /*  3️⃣  Event handling helpers – keep the index in sync                  */
    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void handleCreate(Path p) {
        try {
            if (Files.isDirectory(p)) {
                // A new sub‑directory appeared – we must start watching it
                // (and its sub‑directories, if any) as well.
                registerRecursively(p);
            } else if (Files.isRegularFile(p)) {
                // New file – add to index
                BasicFileAttributes attrs = Files.readAttributes(p, BasicFileAttributes.class);
                String absolute = p.toAbsolutePath().toString();
                index.put(absolute, new FileMeta(absolute, attrs.size(), attrs.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Failed to process CREATE event for " + p + ": " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    private void handleDelete(Path p) {
        // Note: we cannot check whether it was a file or dir – it does not exist.
        // The index contains both files and (if you ever stored dirs) entries. Just remove.
        index.remove(p.toAbsolutePath().toString());
    }

    private void handleModify(Path p) {
        try {
            if (Files.isRegularFile(p)) {
                BasicFileAttributes attrs = Files.readAttributes(p, BasicFileAttributes.class);
                String absolute = p.toAbsolutePath().toString();
                // Overwrite with the fresh attributes
                index.put(absolute, new FileMeta(absolute, attrs.size(), attrs.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Failed to process MODIFY event for " + p + ": " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /*  4️⃣  Fallback full rescans – safety net                               */
    /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void fullRescanRoot(Path root) {
        System.out.println("→ Full rescan of root: " + root);
        // Remove everything that belongs to this root from the index first
        String prefix = root.toAbsolutePath().toString();
        index.keySet().removeIf(path -> path.startsWith(prefix));

        // Re‑index the root from scratch
        try {
            Files.walkFileTree(root, new SimpleFileVisitor<>() {
                @Override
                public FileVisitResult visitFile(Path file, BasicFileAttributes attrs) {
                    String absolute = file.toAbsolutePath().toString();
                    index.put(absolute, new FileMeta(absolute, attrs.size(), attrs.lastModifiedTime().toMillis()));
                    return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                }

                @Override
                public FileVisitResult preVisitDirectory(Path dir, BasicFileAttributes attrs) {
                    // Register the directory for future events (if not already watched)
                    // (We *could* register it again – the OS dedupes.)
                    // The watch registration is done on a dedicated thread that monitors the service,
                    // so we just let the existing logic handle it when the next event occurs.
                    return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                }
            });
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Error during full rescan of " + root + ": " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    /** Convenience – re‑scan all detected drives (used for the periodic safety‑net). */
    private void fullRescanAllDrives() {
        System.out.println("[Periodic] Starting full rescan of all drives …");
        for (File root : DriveDetector.listRootDrives()) {
            fullRescanRoot(root.toPath());
        }
    }
}
```

