## 1️⃣ High‑Level Architecture

```
+-------------------+                               +-------------------+
|  Desktop PC (JVM) |                               |   Android Device |
|-------------------|                               |-------------------|
|  TaskManager      | <--TCP (JSON/Kryo/Java)-->   |  TaskClient       |
|  └─Worker pool    |                               |  └─Worker pool    |
|  (ExecutorService)|                               |  (ExecutorService)|
+-------------------+                               +-------------------+

Legend:
 • Both nodes run the *same* data model (Task, Result)
 • Desktop acts as **coordinator** (accepts connections, load‑balances)
 • Android acts as a **worker** (pulls work, pushes results)
 • All traffic is plain TCP (you can move to TLS later)
```

The diagram can be flipped – you may have Android as the coordinator and the PC as a worker – the code is symmetric. The important thing is to **agree on a wire protocol** and **share the same compiled classes**.

