```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.StandardOpenOption;

/**
 * Helper class that hides all file‑IO for the admin password.
 * The file **admin.txt** contains **only** one line – the SHA‑256 hash
 * of the current admin password.
 */
public final class AdminFile {

    private static final String ADMIN_FILE = "admin.txt";

    /** Returns the hash stored in admin.txt. If the file does not exist
     *  it creates the file with the default password "admin".               */
    public static String readAdminHash() {
        try {
            File f = new File(ADMIN_FILE);
            if (!f.exists()) {
                // first run – create the file with default password "admin"
                String defaultHash = Utility.getHash("admin");
                Files.write(f.toPath(),
                            defaultHash.getBytes(),
                            StandardOpenOption.CREATE);
                return defaultHash;
            }
            // the file contains exactly one line – the hash
            return Files.readAllLines(f.toPath()).get(0).trim();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Unable to read admin file", e);
        }
    }

    /** Overwrites admin.txt with the supplied hash. */
    public static void writeAdminHash(String hash) {
        try {
            Files.write(new File(ADMIN_FILE).toPath(),
                        (hash + System.lineSeparator()).getBytes(),
                        StandardOpenOption.TRUNCATE_EXISTING,
                        StandardOpenOption.CREATE);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Unable to write admin file", e);
        }
    }

    /** Convenience: checks a plain‑text password against the stored hash. */
    public static boolean checkPassword(String plainPassword) {
        String storedHash = readAdminHash();
        String suppliedHash = Utility.getHash(plainPassword);
        return storedHash.equals(suppliedHash);
    }

    private AdminFile() { /* utility class – no instances */ }
}
```

> **Why?**  
> The original `AdminFile` wrote *plain text* “Username: admin / Password: admin”.  
> The specification requires **only the SHA‑256 hash** of the password to be
> stored.  This class centralises that logic and is used by both the admin and
> the game modules.

