## 3️⃣ `TemperatureServlet.java`

```java
package com.example.temperature;

import jakarta.servlet.ServletException;
import jakarta.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import jakarta.servlet.http.*;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import java.text.DecimalFormat;

/**
 * Handles temperature conversion from Celsius to Fahrenheit.
 * URL mapping: /convert
 */
@WebServlet(name = "TemperatureServlet", urlPatterns = {"/convert"})
public class TemperatureServlet extends HttpServlet {

    // Formatter to avoid long floating‑point strings (e.g. 98.60000000001)
    private static final DecimalFormat DF = new DecimalFormat("#.##");

    /**
     * Accept POST requests from the HTML form.
     */
    @Override
    protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp)
            throws ServletException, IOException {

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 1️⃣ Read and validate the user supplied Celsius value
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        String celsiusStr = req.getParameter("celsius");
        double celsius;

        try {
            if (celsiusStr == null || celsiusStr.trim().isEmpty()) {
                throw new NumberFormatException("Empty input");
            }
            celsius = Double.parseDouble(celsiusStr.trim());
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            // Invalid number → redirect back with an error message
            String errorMsg = "Please enter a valid numeric temperature (e.g. 23 or 23.5).";
            resp.sendRedirect(req.getContextPath() + "/index.html?error=" + 
                              java.net.URLEncoder.encode(errorMsg, "UTF-8"));
            return;
        }

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 2️⃣ Convert to Fahrenheit
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        double fahrenheit = celsius * 9.0 / 5.0 + 32.0;

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 3️⃣ Build a friendly comparison message
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        String comparison;
        if (fahrenheit > 32) {
            comparison = "It’s warmer than the freezing point of water (32 °F).";
        } else if (fahrenheit < 32) {
            comparison = "It’s colder than the freezing point of water (32 °F).";
        } else {
            comparison = "Exactly the freezing point of water (32 °F).";
        }

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 4️⃣ Produce the HTML response
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        resp.setContentType("text/html;charset=UTF-8");
        try (PrintWriter out = resp.getWriter()) {
            out.println("<!DOCTYPE html>");
            out.println("<html lang=\"en\"><head>");
            out.println("<meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title>Conversion Result</title>");
            out.println("<style>");
            out.println("body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;margin:2rem;}");
            out.println(".result{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:1rem;background:#f9f9f9;}");
            out.println("</style></head><body>");

            out.println("<h1>Temperature Conversion Result</h1>");
            out.println("<div class=\"result\">");
            out.printf("<p><strong>%.2f °C</strong> equals <strong>%.2f °F</strong></p>%n",
                       celsius, fahrenheit);
            out.println("<p>" + comparison + "</p>");
            out.println("</div>");

            out.println("<p><a href=\"" + req.getContextPath() + "/index.html\">↩️ Back to the form</a></p>");

            out.println("</body></html>");
        }
    }

    /**
     * Optional – allow GET for debugging (just forwards to the form).
     */
    @Override
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp)
            throws ServletException, IOException {
        resp.sendRedirect(req.getContextPath() + "/index.html");
    }
}
```

### What the servlet does:

| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Input read** | `celsius` parameter is obtained from the request. |
| **Validation** | Checks for `null`, empty, or non‑numeric input. If invalid, redirects back to `index.html` with an error query‑string (`?error=…`). |
| **Conversion** | `fahrenheit = celsius * 9 / 5 + 32`. |
| **Comparison message** | Simple logic that tells the user whether the Fahrenheit value is above, below, or exactly 32 °F (freezing point). |
| **HTML response** | Generates a small HTML page with the results and a link back to the form. |

> **Why `@WebServlet`?**  
> The annotation eliminates the need for a servlet entry in `web.xml`. If you prefer the classic XML mapping, see the alternative `web.xml` section below.

