## 6. Service: `FileStorageService`

```java
package com.example.fileupload.service;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.util.StringUtils;
import org.springframework.web.multipart.MultipartFile;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.Objects;

@Service
public class FileStorageService {

    private final Path uploadDir;

    public FileStorageService(@Value("${file.upload-dir}") String uploadDirStr) throws IOException {
        this.uploadDir = Paths.get(uploadDirStr).toAbsolutePath().normalize();

        // Create the directory if it doesn't exist
        Files.createDirectories(this.uploadDir);
    }

    /**
     * Stores the given multipart file on disk.
     *
     * @return the filename under which the file was saved (may be different from the original)
     */
    public String storeFile(MultipartFile file) throws IOException {
        // --- 1. Validate that we actually got a file ---
        if (file.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IOException("Failed to store empty file.");
        }

        // --- 2. Sanitize filename (remove path info, .., etc.) ---
        // Use StringUtils.cleanPath from Spring which also strips any leading/trailing whitespace.
        String originalFilename = StringUtils.cleanPath(Objects.requireNonNull(file.getOriginalFilename()));

        // Re‑reject any filename that still contains suspicious characters after cleaning
        if (originalFilename.contains("..")) {
            throw new IOException("Filename contains invalid path sequence: " + originalFilename);
        }

        // --- 3. Optionally enforce a whitelist of extensions (e.g., only images) ---
        // Uncomment the block below if you need such validation.
        /*
        String ext = com.google.common.io.Files.getFileExtension(originalFilename).toLowerCase();
        if (!Set.of("png", "jpg", "jpeg", "gif", "pdf").contains(ext)) {
            throw new IOException("Unsupported file extension: " + ext);
        }
        */

        // --- 4. Resolve target location (ensure we stay inside the upload dir) ---
        Path targetLocation = this.uploadDir.resolve(originalFilename);

        // If you want to avoid overwriting existing files, generate a unique name:
        // e.g. UUID + original extension
        // String uniqueName = java.util.UUID.randomUUID() + "." + ext;
        // Path targetLocation = this.uploadDir.resolve(uniqueName);

        // --- 5. Copy file data to the target location (replace existing) ---
        Files.copy(file.getInputStream(), targetLocation, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);

        // Return the stored filename (you can also return the absolute path if you want)
        return targetLocation.getFileName().toString();
    }

    public Path getUploadDir() {
        return uploadDir;
    }
}
```

> **Why this service?**  
> * Keeps the controller thin, focuses on HTTP concerns.  
> * Centralises all security checks (filename sanitisation, size checks are already done by Spring).  
> * Makes it easy to swap the storage implementation later (e.g., S3, database).

