### 6.2 `ClientState`

```java
public class ClientState {
    private boolean logged = false;
    private String username = null;

    public void login(String user) { this.username = user; this.logged = true; }
    public void logout() { this.username = null; this.logged = false; }

    public boolean isLogged() { return logged; }
    public String getUsername() { return username; }
}
```

Il client **non** mantiene una sessione sul server; la verifica avviene sul server, ma il client tiene traccia se è “loggato” per decidere quali comandi può chiedere all’utente (es. non mostrare `insertReview` prima del login).

### 6.3 Loop principale

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    String host = "localhost";
    int port = 5000;   // o valore da args

    try (Socket socket = new Socket(host, port);
         PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(socket.getOutputStream(), true);
         BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(
                 new InputStreamReader(socket.getInputStream()));
         BufferedReader console = new BufferedReader(
                 new InputStreamReader(System.in))) {

        ClientState state = new ClientState();
        System.out.println("Benvenuto su HOTELIER. Digita 'help' per i comandi.");

        while (true) {
            System.out.print("> ");
            String line = console.readLine();
            if (line == null) break; // EOF

            if (line.trim().equalsIgnoreCase("quit")) {
                send(out, in, new Request("quit", null));
                break;
            }

            if (line.trim().equalsIgnoreCase("help")) {
                printHelp(state);
                continue;
            }

            Request req = CommandParser.parse(line, state);
            if (req == null) continue; // comando non valido, messaggio già stampato

            Response resp = send(out, in, req);
            UIPrinter.print(resp, state);
        }

    } catch (IOException e) {
        e.printStackTrace();
    }
}
```

### 6.4 `CommandParser`

```java
public class CommandParser {

    public static Request parse(String line, ClientState state) {
        String[] parts = line.trim().split("\\s+");
        String cmd = parts[0].toLowerCase();

        switch (cmd) {
            case "register":
                if (parts.length != 3) {
                    System.out.println("Uso: register <username> <password>");
                    return null;
                }
                JsonObject payloadR = new JsonObject();
                payloadR.addProperty("username", parts[1]);
                payloadR.addProperty("password", parts[2]);
                return new Request("register", payloadR);

            case "login":
                if (parts.length != 3) {
                    System.out.println("Uso: login <username> <password>");
                    return null;
                }
                JsonObject payloadL = new JsonObject();
                payloadL.addProperty("username", parts[1]);
                payloadL.addProperty("password", parts[2]);
                return new Request("login", payloadL);

            case "logout":
                return new Request("logout", null);

            case "searchhotel":
                if (parts.length != 3) {
                    System.out.println("Uso: searchHotel <nomeHotel> <città>");
                    return null;
                }
                JsonObject payloadS = new JsonObject();
                payloadS.addProperty("nomeHotel", parts[1]);
                payloadS.addProperty("città", parts[2]);
                return new Request("searchHotel", payloadS);

            case "searchall":
                if (parts.length != 2) {
                    System.out.println("Uso: searchAllHotels <città>");
                    return null;
                }
                JsonObject payloadA = new JsonObject();
                payloadA.addProperty("città", parts[1]);
                return new Request("searchAllHotels", payloadA);

            case "insertreview":
                if (!state.isLogged()) {
                    System.out.println("Devi essere loggato per inserire una review.");
                    return null;
                }
                // sintassi: insertReview <nomeHotel> <città> <globalScore> <s1> <s2> ... <sn>
                if (parts.length < 5) {
                    System.out.println("Uso: insertReview <nomeHotel> <città> <globalScore> <s1> <s2> ...");
                    return null;
                }
                JsonObject payloadI = new JsonObject();
                payloadI.addProperty("nomeHotel", parts[1]);
                payloadI.addProperty("nomeCittà", parts[2]);
                payloadI.addProperty("GlobalScore", Integer.parseInt(parts[3]));
                JsonArray arr = new JsonArray();
                for (int i = 4; i < parts.length; i++) {
                    arr.add(Integer.parseInt(parts[i]));
                }
                payloadI.add("SingleScores", arr);
                return new Request("insertReview", payloadI);

            case "showmybadges":
                return new Request("showMyBadges", null);

            default:
                System.out.println("Comando non riconosciuto. Digita 'help' per la lista.");
                return null;
        }
    }
}
```

