## 4️⃣  Optional – **Pinned‑Certificate TrustManager** (production‑ready)

If you want to lock the client to a specific certificate (or CA) that is shipped with the app → put the PEM/DER file into `res/raw/` and load it:

```java
import android.content.Context;
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.security.KeyStore;
import java.security.cert.CertificateFactory;
import java.security.cert.X509Certificate;
import javax.net.ssl.TrustManagerFactory;
import javax.net.ssl.X509TrustManager;

public final class PinnedTrustManager {

    /**
     * Creates a TrustManager that trusts only the certificate stored in raw resources.
     *
     * @param ctx          Android context
     * @param rawResId     resource id of the PEM/DER certificate (e.g. R.raw.my_server_cert)
     * @return a X509TrustManager you can give to SecureTcpClient
     */
    public static X509TrustManager create(Context ctx, int rawResId) throws Exception {
        // 1️⃣ Load the certificate (PEM or DER)
        CertificateFactory cf = CertificateFactory.getInstance("X.509");
        InputStream certIs = ctx.getResources().openRawResource(rawResId);
        X509Certificate cert = (X509Certificate) cf.generateCertificate(certIs);
        certIs.close();

        // 2️⃣ Put it into a new KeyStore
        KeyStore ks = KeyStore.getInstance(KeyStore.getDefaultType());
        ks.load(null); // initialise empty keystore
        ks.setCertificateEntry("pinned", cert);

        // 3️⃣ Build a TrustManagerFactory from that keystore
        TrustManagerFactory tmf = TrustManagerFactory.getInstance(
                TrustManagerFactory.getDefaultAlgorithm());
        tmf.init(ks);

        // 4️⃣ Return the first X509TrustManager (there will be exactly one)
        for (javax.net.ssl.TrustManager tm : tmf.getTrustManagers()) {
            if (tm instanceof X509TrustManager) {
                return (X509TrustManager) tm;
            }
        }
        throw new IllegalStateException("No X509TrustManager found");
    }
}
```

Usage in `MainActivity`:

```java
try {
    X509TrustManager pinned = PinnedTrustManager.create(this, R.raw.my_server_cert);
    client.setCustomTrustManager(pinned);
} catch (Exception e) {
    Log.e(TAG, "Failed to load pinned cert", e);
}
```

