## 7️⃣ Extending the example (what you might do next)

| Feature | How to add it |
|---------|---------------|
| **Multiple entities (e.g., Department, Project)** | Create more `@Entity` classes, add them to `MetadataSources` (`sources.addAnnotatedClass(Department.class)`). |
| **One‑to‑Many / Many‑to‑One** | Use `@OneToMany`, `@ManyToOne`, and `mappedBy`/`joinColumn`. |
| **DAO / Repository pattern** | Wrap session operations in a `EmployeeDao` class; inject the `SessionFactory` via Spring or CDI. |
| **Spring Boot integration** | Drop `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa` and `com.h2database:h2`; Spring auto‑configures the `EntityManagerFactory`. |
| **SQL script initialization** | Place `import.sql` in `src/main/resources`; Hibernate automatically runs it if `hibernate.hbm2ddl.auto` is `create`/`update`. |
| **Connection pool tuning (c3p0 / HikariCP)** | Add the pool library to `pom.xml` and set pool properties (`hibernate.c3p0.*` or `hibernate.hikari.*`). |
| **Unit tests with JUnit** | Use `@BeforeAll` to build `SessionFactory`, and `@AfterAll` to shut it down. Use a transaction that rolls back after each test (`@Transactional` in Spring or manual rollback). |

