## 2. The Remote Interface (Encyclopedia.java)

```java
package rmi;

import java.rmi.Remote;
import java.rmi.RemoteException;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

/**
 * Remote methods that the client can invoke.
 */
public interface Encyclopedia extends Remote {

    /** Total number of characters (including spaces) in the 300‑word text. */
    int Count() throws RemoteException;

    /** Set of words that appear more than once. */
    List<String> repeatedwords() throws RemoteException;

    /** The longest word (if several have same length, any one is returned). */
    String longest() throws RemoteException;

    /** The shortest word (if several have same length, any one is returned). */
    String shortest() throws RemoteException;

    /** Word → occurrence count for every distinct word. */
    Map<String,Integer> Repeat() throws RemoteException;

    /** --------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Helpers for the client to request the *timed* versions.
     *  Both return a simple wrapper that contains the result + runtime.
     * -------------------------------------------------------------- */
    ResultWrapper runNonThreaded() throws RemoteException;
    ResultWrapper runThreaded()    throws RemoteException;

    /** Small POJO used to transport result + elapsed time. */
    class ResultWrapper implements java.io.Serializable {
        private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
        public final String   description;   // Human readable description of the run
        public final long     elapsedMs;      // elapsed time in ms
        public final int      count;
        public final List<String> repeated;
        public final String   longest;
        public final String   shortest;
        public final Map<String,Integer> repeatMap;

        public ResultWrapper(String description, long elapsedMs,
                             int count, List<String> repeated,
                             String longest, String shortest,
                             Map<String,Integer> repeatMap) {
            this.description = description;
            this.elapsedMs    = elapsedMs;
            this.count        = count;
            this.repeated     = repeated;
            this.longest      = longest;
            this.shortest     = shortest;
            this.repeatMap    = repeatMap;
        }
    }
}
```

The interface declares the **five analysis methods** and, for convenience, two extra methods (`runNonThreaded()` and `runThreaded()`) that execute **all** analyses and return a `ResultWrapper` containing both the data *and* the elapsed time. This makes it very easy for the GUI to display the timings.

