Below is a **self‑contained, reusable** Java utility that

1. **parses an XML document that lives in a `String`**,  
2. **selects one (or many) sub‑trees with an XPath expression**,  
3. **converts the selected `Node`/`NodeList` back to a `String`** (i.e. the exact XML fragment you want).

The code works with plain JDK (no external libraries) and is safe for both normal and namespaced XML.  
If you need a quick‑and‑dirty solution you can also use **Jsoup** (HTML‑style parsing) or **StAX**, but for full‑XML compliance the DOM + XPath approach is the most robust.

---

## 1️⃣ The core utility class

```java
package com.example.xmlutil;

import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import javax.xml.xpath.*;
import javax.xml.transform.*;
import javax.xml.transform.dom.DOMSource;
import javax.xml.transform.stream.StreamResult;

import org.w3c.dom.*;

import java.io.*;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * Utility to extract a piece of XML (or many pieces) from an XML string
 * using an XPath expression.
 *
 * <p>Typical usage:
 *
 * <pre>{@code
 * String xml          = "...";               // the whole document
 * String xpathExpr    = "//book[@id='b2']";   // what you want
 *
 * // returns a single fragment (null if nothing matches)
 * String fragment = XmlExtractor.extractFirst(xml, xpathExpr);
 *
 * // returns all fragments that match the expression
 * List<String> fragments = XmlExtractor.extractAll(xml, xpathExpr);
 * }</pre>
 *
 * <p>The returned strings are *exactly* the XML of the matched node(s) –
 * including their start‑ and end‑tags, attributes, namespaces, etc.
 *
 * @author  ChatGPT (2024)
 */
public final class XmlExtractor {

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Private constructor – this class is not meant to be instantiated
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    private XmlExtractor() {
        // static‑only
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Public API ------------------------------------------------------------
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    /**
     * Returns the XML fragment of the **first** node that matches the given
     * XPath expression, or {@code null} if the expression matches nothing.
     *
     * @param xmlString   the complete XML document as a {@code String}
     * @param xpathExpr   an XPath expression (e.g. "//book[@id='b2']")
     * @return the XML of the first matching node, or {@code null}
     * @throws Exception  if parsing or XPath evaluation fails
     */
    public static String extractFirst(String xmlString, String xpathExpr) throws Exception {
        Node node = evaluateSingleNode(xmlString, xpathExpr);
        return (node == null) ? null : nodeToString(node);
    }

    /**
     * Returns a {@code List<String>} where each entry is the XML of a node
     * that matches the XPath expression. If nothing matches, an empty list
     * is returned.
     *
     * @param xmlString   the complete XML document as a {@code String}
     * @param xpathExpr   an XPath expression
     * @return list of XML fragments (may be empty)
     * @throws Exception  if parsing or XPath evaluation fails
     */
    public static List<String> extractAll(String xmlString, String xpathExpr) throws Exception {
        NodeList nodes = evaluateNodeList(xmlString, xpathExpr);
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>(nodes.getLength());

        for (int i = 0; i < nodes.getLength(); i++) {
            result.add(nodeToString(nodes.item(i)));
        }
        return result;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Implementation helpers -------------------------------------------------
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    /** Parses the XML string into a W3C Document (namespace‑aware). */
    private static Document parseXml(String xmlString) throws Exception {
        DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
        // Important – many XMLs use namespaces; keep it on
        dbf.setNamespaceAware(true);
        // Prevent XXE attacks (good practice even for internal strings)
        dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
        dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
        dbf.setXIncludeAware(false);
        dbf.setExpandEntityReferences(false);

        DocumentBuilder db = dbf.newDocumentBuilder();
        try (StringReader sr = new StringReader(xmlString)) {
            InputSource is = new InputSource(sr);
            return db.parse(is);
        }
    }

    /** Compiles the XPath expression once (thread‑safe after compilation). */
    private static XPathExpression compileXPath(String xpathExpr) throws XPathExpressionException {
        XPathFactory xpf = XPathFactory.newInstance();
        XPath xpath = xpf.newXPath();
        // If you need namespace prefixes in XPath, set a NamespaceContext here:
        // xpath.setNamespaceContext(myNamespaceContext);
        return xpath.compile(xpathExpr);
    }

    /** Returns the first node that matches the XPath expression, or {@code null}. */
    private static Node evaluateSingleNode(String xmlString, String xpathExpr) throws Exception {
        Document doc = parseXml(xmlString);
        XPathExpression expr = compileXPath(xpathExpr);
        // XPathConstants.NODE returns the *first* matching node
        return (Node) expr.evaluate(doc, XPathConstants.NODE);
    }

    /** Returns a NodeList (maybe empty) for the XPath expression. */
    private static NodeList evaluateNodeList(String xmlString, String xpathExpr) throws Exception {
        Document doc = parseXml(xmlString);
        XPathExpression expr = compileXPath(xpathExpr);
        // XPathConstants.NODESET returns *all* matching nodes
        return (NodeList) expr.evaluate(doc, XPathConstants.NODESET);
    }

    /** Serialises a DOM {@link Node} (including its children) back to a String. */
    private static String nodeToString(Node node) throws Exception {
        // The Transformer will omit the XML declaration (<?xml ...?>) for fragments,
        // which is usually what you want.
        TransformerFactory tf = TransformerFactory.newInstance();
        // Prevent external entity injection in the transformer as well
        tf.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
        Transformer transformer = tf.newTransformer();

        // Optional: pretty‑print the fragment (indentation)
        transformer.setOutputProperty(OutputKeys.OMIT_XML_DECLARATION, "yes");
        transformer.setOutputProperty(OutputKeys.INDENT, "yes");
        // Amount of indentation – works with the built‑in Xalan implementation
        transformer.setOutputProperty("{http://xml.apache.org/xslt}indent-amount", "2");

        // Some Node types (e.g. Attr, Text) cannot be transformed directly, so we
        // wrap them in a dummy document fragment when needed.
        DOMSource source;
        if (node.getNodeType() == Node.ATTRIBUTE_NODE ||
            node.getNodeType() == Node.TEXT_NODE ||
            node.getNodeType() == Node.COMMENT_NODE) {
            Document dummy = node.getOwnerDocument().implementation.createDocument(null, null, null);
            dummy.appendChild(dummy.importNode(node, true));
            source = new DOMSource(dummy);
        } else {
            source = new DOMSource(node);
        }

        StringWriter writer = new StringWriter();
        StreamResult result = new StreamResult(writer);
        transformer.transform(source, result);
        return writer.toString().trim(); // trim to drop leading newline from indentation
    }
}
```

### What the class does

| Step | Reason |
|------|--------|
| **Parse XML → `Document`** | Turns the raw string into a proper DOM tree. |
| **Compile XPath** | Re‑usable, fast, and lets you select any node(s). |
| **Evaluate** (`NODE` or `NODESET`) | `extractFirst` returns the first hit; `extractAll` returns every hit. |
| **Transform `Node` → String** | Uses a `Transformer` (JAXP) to serialise the fragment *exactly* as XML (no XML declaration, optional pretty‑print). |
| **Security hardening** | Disables external entity loading (XXE) for both parser and transformer. |

