        .add("bk", "http://example.com/book");

String fragment = XmlExtractor.extractFirst(xml,
        "//bk:book[@id='b2']", ns);   // overload you add that passes nsCtx
```

Feel free to copy the `SimpleNamespaceContext` into your project – it is only ~30 lines of code and works for any number of prefixes.

