| Feature | How it works |
|--------|--------------|
| **Grid world** | 20 × 12 ASCII tiles (`.` empty, `P` player, `S` gold stash, `Z` zombie). |
| **Play button** | Randomly spawns the player and starts the day/night loop. |
| **Gold stash placement** | Click *Place Gold* → click any tile on the grid to drop a stash. |
| **Day‑Night cycle** | 30 s day → 30 s night (configurable). |
| **Zombie waves** | At night zombies spawn on random edges if at least one stash exists. |
| **AI** | Zombies move one tile per tick toward the *closest* stash (Manhattan distance). |
| **Destruction** | When a zombie reaches a stash the stash disappears. |
| **Clean & modern** | ES2022+, private fields, static helpers, arrow functions, `requestAnimationFrame` for rendering, `Map` for fast look‑ups. |

---  

## 2️⃣  The code  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>ASCII Tower‑Defense</title>
<style>
  body {font-family: monospace; background:#111; color:#ddd; text-align:center;}
  #grid {line-height:1.2; user-select:none; cursor:default;}
  button {margin: .5rem; padding:.5rem 1rem; font-size:1rem;}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>ASCII Tower‑Defense</h1>
<button id="playBtn">Play</button>
<button id="goldBtn" disabled>Place Gold</button>
<pre id="grid"></pre>

<script type="module">
/* ------------ Constants & Helpers ------------ */
const TILE = { EMPTY: '.', PLAYER: 'P', STASH: 'S', ZOMBIE: 'Z' };
const DAY_MS   = 30_000;   // 30 s day
const NIGHT_MS = 30_000;   // 30 s night
const SPAWN_INTERVAL = 4_000; // zombies every 4 s at night

/* ------------ Grid ------------ */
class Grid {
  #cells;
  constructor(public w = 20, public h = 12) {
    this.#cells = Array.from({ length: h }, () => Array(w).fill(TILE.EMPTY));
  }
  get(x, y) { return this.#cells[y]?.[x]; }
  set(x, y, v) { if (this.inBounds(x, y)) this.#cells[y][x] = v; }
  inBounds(x, y) { return x >= 0 && x < this.w && y >= 0 && y < this.h; }
  toString() { return this.#cells.map(r => r.join('')).join('\n'); }
}

/* ------------ Entities ------------ */
class Entity {
  constructor(public x, public y) {}
}
class Player extends Entity { static ICON = TILE.PLAYER; }
class GoldStash extends Entity { static ICON = TILE.STASH; }
class Zombie extends Entity { static ICON = TILE.ZOMBIE; }

/* ------------ Game Core ------------ */
class Game {
  #grid = new Grid();
  #player = null;
  #stashes = new Map();   // key: `${x},${y}` -> GoldStash
  #zombies = new Map();   // key: `${x},${y}` -> Zombie
  #day = true;
  #running = false;
  #dayTimer = null;
  #nightTimer = null;
  #spawnTimer = null;
  #renderRAF = null;

  constructor(private renderCB) {}

  /* ----- Public API ----- */
  start() {
    if (this.#running) return;
    this.#running = true;
    this.#reset();
    this.#spawnPlayer();
    this.#toggleDayNight();           // start with day
    this.#renderLoop();
  }

  placeStash(x, y) {
    if (!this.#grid.inBounds(x, y) || this.#grid.get(x, y) !== TILE.EMPTY) return;
    const stash = new GoldStash(x, y);
    this.#stashes.set(`${x},${y}`, stash);
    this.#grid.set(x, y, GoldStash.ICON);
  }

  /* ----- Internals ----- */
  #reset() {
    this.#grid = new Grid();
    this.#player = null;
    this.#stashes.clear();
    this.#zombies.clear();
    clearTimeout(this.#dayTimer);
    clearTimeout(this.#nightTimer);
    clearInterval(this.#spawnTimer);
  }

  #spawnPlayer() {
    const x = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.#grid.w);
    const y = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.#grid.h);
    this.#player = new Player(x, y);
    this.#grid.set(x, y, Player.ICON);
  }

  #toggleDayNight() {
    this.#day = !this.#day;
    if (this.#day) {
      // Day → schedule night
      this.#dayTimer = setTimeout(() => this.#toggleDayNight(), DAY_MS);
    } else {
      // Night → schedule day + start zombie spawns
      this.#nightTimer = setTimeout(() => this.#toggleDayNight(), NIGHT_MS);
      if (this.#stashes.size) this.#spawnTimer = setInterval(() => this.#spawnZombie(), SPAWN_INTERVAL);
    }
  }

  #spawnZombie() {
    if (!this.#stashes.size) return;
    // pick random edge cell
    const edge = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 'h' : 'v';
    let x, y;
    if (edge === 'h') {      // top/bottom
      x = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.#grid.w);
      y = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 0 : this.#grid.h - 1;
    } else {                // left/right
      y = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.#grid.h);
      x = Math.random() < 0.5 ? 0 : this.#grid.w - 1;
    }
    if (this.#grid.get(x, y) !== TILE.EMPTY) return; // occupied → skip
    const zombie = new Zombie(x, y);
    this.#zombies.set(`${x},${y}`, zombie);
    this.#grid.set(x, y, Zombie.ICON);
  }

  #moveZombies() {
    if (!this.#zombies.size) return;
    const newZombies = new Map();

    for (const [key, zombie] of this.#zombies) {
      const { x, y } = zombie;
      // find nearest stash (Manhattan)
      let target = null, minDist = Infinity;
      for (const stash of this.#stashes.values()) {
        const d = Math.abs(stash.x - x) + Math.abs(stash.y - y);
        if (d < minDist) { minDist = d; target = stash; }
      }
      if (!target) continue; // no stash left → zombie idle

      // step towards target
      const nx = x + Math.sign(target.x - x);
      const ny = y + Math.sign(target.y - y);
      const newKey = `${nx},${ny}`;

      // clear old cell
      this.#grid.set(x, y, TILE.EMPTY);

      // check collision with stash
      if (this.#grid.get(nx, ny) === GoldStash.ICON) {
        // destroy stash
        this.#stashes.delete(newKey);
        // zombie stays on the stash cell (remains alive)
      }

      // place zombie (overwrite anything else)
      this.#grid.set(nx, ny, Zombie.ICON);
      newZombies.set(newKey, new Zombie(nx, ny));
    }
    this.#zombies = newZombies;
  }

  #renderLoop() {
    this.#moveZombies();          // one step per frame (≈60 fps is fine)
    this.renderCB(this.#grid.toString(), this.#day);
    this.#renderRAF = requestAnimationFrame(() => this.#renderLoop());
  }

  stop() {
    this.#running = false;
    cancelAnimationFrame(this.#renderRAF);
    clearTimeout(this.#dayTimer);
    clearTimeout(this.#nightTimer);
    clearInterval(this.#spawnTimer);
  }
}

/* ------------ UI wiring ------------ */
const gridEl = document.getElementById('grid');
const playBtn = document.getElementById('playBtn');
const goldBtn = document.getElementById('goldBtn');

let game = null;
let placingGold = false;

/* render callback */
function render(gridStr, isDay) {
  gridEl.textContent = gridStr;
  gridEl.style.color = isDay ? '#8f8' : '#f88';
}

/* Play button */
playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  if (game) game.stop();
  game = new Game(render);
  game.start();
  goldBtn.disabled = false;
});

/* Gold button */
goldBtn.addEventListener('click', () => placingGold = !placingGold);
goldBtn.textContent = 'Place Gold';

/* Grid clicking – place stash */
gridEl.addEventListener('click', e => {
  if (!placingGold || !game) return;
  const rect = gridEl.getBoundingClientRect();
  const charW = rect.width / game?.#grid?.w; // approximate char width
  const charH = rect.height / game?.#grid?.h;
  const x = Math.floor((e.clientX - rect.left) / charW);
  const y = Math.floor((e.clientY - rect.top) / charH);
  game.placeStash(x, y);
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---  

## 3️⃣  How it works (short walkthrough)

1. **`Grid`** holds a 2‑D array of single‑character tiles and provides a fast `toString()` for rendering.
2. **`Entity`** is the base for `Player`, `GoldStash`, and `Zombie`. Each stores its `x`/`y` position.
3. **`Game`** owns the grid and three `Map`s:
   * `#stashes` – all gold storages,
   * `#zombies` – all living zombies,
   * `#player` – the single player sprite.
4. **Day/Night** toggles every `DAY_MS` / `NIGHT_MS`. When night starts and a stash exists a `setInterval` spawns zombies on random edges.
5. **Zombie AI** – each frame (via `requestAnimationFrame`) every zombie looks for the closest stash (Manhattan distance) and moves one step toward it. Upon reaching a stash the stash disappears.
6. **Rendering** – a simple `<pre>` shows the grid. Day/night changes the text colour (`#8f8` vs `#f88`).
7. **Controls** –  
   * **Play** → random player placement & start loops.  
   * **Place Gold** toggles placement mode; clicking the grid drops a stash at the clicked cell.

---  

### Tweaking & Extending  

| Want to… | Simple change |
|----------|----------------|
| Change map size | Edit `new Grid(width, height)` inside `Game` (or expose UI). |
| Faster zombies | Call `#moveZombies()` less frequently (e.g., every 2 frames). |
| More zombie types | Create subclasses of `Zombie` and add a spawn‑type selector. |
| Show a countdown | Add another DOM element and update it in the day‑night timer callbacks. |

The core loop, data structures, and class layout are already modular, so adding features keeps the code clean. Have fun defending your gold!

