## 7. Security & Production Tips

| Concern | Recommendation |
|---------|----------------|
| **Store secrets safely** | Use a proper secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager, Vault, etc.) for production. |
| **HTTPS** | Never serve the API over plain HTTP in production. Deploy behind an SSL‑terminating load balancer or use services like **Render**, **Fly.io**, **Heroku**, **Vercel**, etc. |
| **Rate‑limit / brute‑force protection** | Add `express-rate-limit` or similar to `/login` & `/register`. |
| **Password policy** | Enforce a stronger policy (uppercase, numbers, symbols) and consider `zxcvbn` strength estimator. |
| **Refresh tokens** | For long‑living sessions consider adding a refresh‑token flow rather than very long JWT expiry. |
| **CORS** | Tighten the `origin` whitelist for your front‑end domain. |
| **Account verification** | Send an email verification link before allowing login (nodemailer, SendGrid, etc.). |
| **Account lockout** | After N failed attempts, temporarily lock the account to stop credential stuffing. |
| **Logging** | Use a structured logger (pino, winston) and log authentication events for audit. |
| **Deploy** | Dockerise the app (create a `Dockerfile`) – makes it portable to any cloud provider. |

