The approach is a **two‑step feature matrix**:

| Step | What we test                                            | How we test it                         |
|------|---------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|
| 1️⃣   | *Value‑based* features – objects, methods, globals      | `typeof …`, `'property' in obj` etc.   |
| 2️⃣   | *Syntax* features – operators, literals, new keywords   | `new Function('…')` inside a `try / catch` so that we never throw a syntax error in the surrounding code. |

If **any** test fails, the function returns `false`; otherwise it returns `true`.

> **Why this is better than a simple “user‑agent” check?**  
> User‑agent strings are unreliable and quickly become outdated. Feature detection works even on *future* browsers that may still be reported as “old” by their UA string.

---

## 📦 The complete function

