Below is a **complete, minimal example** of a small website that uses **HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and PHP**.  
You can copy the files into a folder (e.g., `my‑site/`) and run them on any web‑server that supports PHP (e.g., XAMPP, MAMP, LAMP, Docker, etc.).

---

## 1️⃣ Project structure

```
my-site/
│
├─ index.html          # the main page (HTML)
├─ style.css           # styling (CSS)
├─ script.js           # client‑side logic (JavaScript)
└─ process.php         # server‑side handler (PHP)
```

> **Tip:** If you use a local dev stack (XAMPP/MAMP/Docker) place the folder inside the server’s document root (`htdocs` for XAMPP, `www` for MAMP, etc.) and open `http://localhost/my‑site/index.html`.

---

## 2️⃣ `index.html` – the page layout

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Simple JS‑CSS‑PHP Demo</title>

    <!-- Link to CSS -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">

    <!-- Link to JavaScript (deferred so the DOM loads first) -->
    <script src="script.js" defer></script>
</head>
