.\client.ps1
```

If you want to connect to a remote host or a different port, pass the URI:

```powershell
.\client.ps1 -Uri "ws://192.168.1.42:8080"
```

You’ll see a prompt:

```
✅ Connected! Type your messages below. Press Ctrl+C to quit.
```

Type a message, press **Enter**, and you’ll instantly see it echoed back, prefixed with a timestamp. All other client windows will see the same line.

