## 2️⃣  Data Model Design (Schema)

Below is a **sample logical schema** that works well for a small‑to‑medium blog.  
Feel free to add more object stores (e.g., `settings`, `drafts`) later.

```text
Database: myBlogDB
Version: 1

Object Store: posts
  - keyPath: "id" (auto‑increment)
  - indexes:
      title      (unique: false)
      slug       (unique: true)   // URL friendly
      authorId   (unique: false)
      createdAt  (unique: false)
      tags       (multiEntry: true)
      fullText   (unique: false) // optional, for simple full‑text

Object Store: authors
  - keyPath: "id" (auto‑increment)
