## 7. Optional enhancements (you may add later)

| Feature | How to implement (short hint) |
|---------|------------------------------|
| **Limit name length** / **filter profanity** | Add `if (name.length > 20) …` or use a small list of banned words before sending the request. |
| **Show the full list, not just top‑10** | Remove the `slice(0,10)` or add a “Show all” button that toggles a larger table. |
| **Add timestamps** | Store `Date.now()` in the PHP file (`name|score|timestamp`) and format it on the client side. |
| **Better UI** | Replace the inline CSS with a separate stylesheet, add animations for the modal, use `:focus` styling for the input, etc. |
| **Server‑side language other than PHP** | The same logic works with Node (`express`), Python (`Flask`), Go, etc.; only the endpoint changes. |
| **Prevent duplicate names/score combos** | In `save_score.php` you could first read the file, check if the same line already exists, and skip appending. |
| **Protect against script injection** | Escape `|` and HTML‑encode the name before writing it (or use `json_encode`). |

