| **UI Action** | The **Action name** (function) matches the script (`attachMany`). The list button appears on the list header. |
| **UI Page** | Its **ID** (`attach_many_modal`) matches the name passed to `new GlideModal('attach_many_modal')`. |
| **Script Include** | `Client Callable = true` (otherwise GlideAjax will reject the call). |
| **Permissions** | Users need `read` on the target table *and* the `attachment` role (or the permission to add attachments). If you’re in a scoped app, make sure the Script Include is in the same scope or is set to **"Accessible from all applications"**. |
| **Test** | 1️⃣ Go to the list, select 2‑3 rows, click the **Attach document to many** button. 2️⃣ Choose a PDF (or any file) → **Submit**. 3️⃣ You should see a success message and, after the modal closes, the attachment appears on **each** of the selected records (open any of them to verify). |

---

## 5. (Optional) Make the Action **Declarative** with Action Builder (UI‑Builder)

If you are building a **Workspace/Service Portal** UI using the *Action Builder*:

1. **Create an Action** (type = *List Action*) and set its **Client Script** exactly as the UI Action script above (just copy the `attachMany()` body).  
