```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Click to Change Background Colour</title>
    <style>
        /* Basic page styling – feel free to modify */
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 2rem;
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            transition: background-color 0.4s ease;  /* smooth colour fade */
        }

        .centered {
            max-width: 400px;
            margin: 5rem auto;
            text-align: center;
        }

        button {
            padding: .8rem 1.5rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
            cursor: pointer;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            background: #333;
            color: #fff;
        }

        button:hover {
            background: #555;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="centered">
    <h1>Click anywhere to change the background colour</h1>
    <p>Or press the button below.</p>
    <button id="changeBtn">Change colour</button>
</div>

<script>
    /**
     * Generates a random colour in hexadecimal format, e.g. "#3FA9C2"
     */
    function getRandomHexColor() {
        // Math.random() → 0 ≤ x < 1
        // Multiply by 0xFFFFFF (= 16777215) and floor to get an integer
        const randomInt = Math.floor(Math.random() * 0xFFFFFF);
        // Convert to hex and pad with leading zeros if necessary
        const hex = randomInt.toString(16).padStart(6, '0');
        return `#${hex}`;
    }

    /**
     * Sets a new random colour as the document body background.
     */
    function changeBackground() {
        document.body.style.backgroundColor = getRandomHexColor();
    }

    // 1️⃣ Click anywhere on the page (except the button) → change colour
    document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
        // If the click originated from the button we’ll handle it there,
        // otherwise change the colour.
        if (!event.target.closest('#changeBtn')) {
            changeBackground();
        }
    });

    // 2️⃣ Click the explicit button → also change colour
    document.getElementById('changeBtn').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        // Prevent the event from bubbling up to the document listener
        // (so we don’t change the colour twice on the same click)
        e.stopPropagation();
        changeBackground();
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
| Part | What it does |
|------|--------------|
| **HTML** | Provides a small UI (a heading, a paragraph and a button). |
| **CSS** | Gives the page a pleasant look and adds a smooth transition when the background colour changes (`transition: background-color 0.4s`). |
| **JavaScript** | <ul><li>`getRandomHexColor()` creates a random 6‑digit hex colour.</li><li>`changeBackground()` assigns that colour to `document.body.style.backgroundColor`.</li><li>An event listener on the whole document reacts to clicks (except when the click is on the button).</li><li>A second listener on the button also triggers the colour change, and `e.stopPropagation()` prevents the click from bubbling up to the document listener, avoiding a double‑change.</li></ul> |

Feel free to tweak the code:

