| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| **Attaching `logger` to the `app` object** works, but you lose type‑checking and you’ll repeatedly import the same logger in other modules. | Use **dependency injection** (pass `logger` into route factories) *or* expose it via a **singleton** (`src/core/Logger`). If you keep the property, set it **after** all middlewares so that any `app.use` that expects `app.logger` is safe. |
| **`app.logger` will be undefined in tests** unless you import the same boot file. | Export the logger **separately**: `module.exports = { app, logger }`. That makes unit‑testing easier. |

