### What the script does

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1. Connect** | `mysqli` connection is opened once at the top. |
| **2. CSRF token** | A random token stored in `$_SESSION` and echoed as a hidden field. |
| **3. Form submission** | When `$_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST'` the script runs validation. |
| **4. Validation** | - Required fields <br> - Email format <br> - Simple phone regex <br> - Password and confirmation match <br> - Gender must be one of the three options |
| **5. Password hashing** | `password_hash()` (default bcrypt) – the only safe way to store passwords. |
| **6. Prepared INSERT** | `INSERT INTO students … VALUES (?,?,?,?,?)` – placeholders are bound with `$stmt->bind_param()`. No user‑supplied value ever appears directly in the query. |
| **7. Success / error feedback** | Message printed above the form. The form fields keep the previously entered values (except passwords) so the user doesn’t have to re‑type everything on error. |
| **8. HTML** | Clean, minimal CSS, required attributes, correct input types (`text`, `email`, `tel`, `password`). |

