## 4️⃣ Quick checklist before you go live

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **Password** | Stored with `password_hash()`. Use `password_verify()` when users log in. |
| **SQL Injection** | Eliminated by using prepared statements (`?` placeholders). |
| **XSS** | All output that originates from the user (`$name`, `$email`, $errors…) is escaped with `htmlspecialchars()`. |
| **CSRF** | A simple token stored in session is verified on POST. |
| **Unique e‑mail** | `UNIQUE` constraint in table plus handling of MySQL error 1062. |
| **HTTPS** | Deploy the page under HTTPS – otherwise passwords travel in clear text. |
| **Error logging** | In production replace `die()` / raw `echo` with logging to a file and show a generic message to the visitor. |

