## 2. Database – Create the Table

Save the following as `db.sql` and run it (e.g. via phpMyAdmin, MySQL Workbench or the command line).

```sql
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS demo_auth CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
USE demo_auth;

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
    id          BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    username    VARCHAR(50)   NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    email       VARCHAR(255)  NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password    VARCHAR(255)  NOT NULL,
    created_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
```

> **Why these columns?**  
> *`username`* and *`email`* are both unique so we can prevent duplicate accounts.  
> *`password`* stores a **hash** (never the plain text).  
