## 4. CSRF Helper (`csrf.php`)

Cross‑Site Request Forgery protection is trivial with a token stored in the session.

```php
<?php
// csrf.php – include wherever you need a token
session_start();

function csrf_token(): string {
    if (empty($_SESSION['csrf'])) {
        // 32‑byte random string, base64‑encoded
        $_SESSION['csrf'] = bin2hex(random_bytes(32));
    }
    return $_SESSION['csrf'];
}

function csrf_check(): bool {
    if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] !== 'POST') {
        return false;
    }
    $posted = $_POST['csrf'] ?? '';
    return hash_equals($_SESSION['csrf'] ?? '', $posted);
}
```

In every form we’ll add:

```html
<input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?php echo htmlspecialchars(csrf_token()); ?>">
```

And right after processing a POST we’ll call `csrf_check()`.

