## 10. Security Checklist – What to Double‑Check Before Going Live

| ✅ | Item | Why |
|----|------|-----|
| ✅ | **Use HTTPS** everywhere | Prevents eavesdropping (passwords, session cookies). |
| ✅ | **`session.cookie_secure = true`** (if HTTPS) | Cookie sent only over TLS. |
| ✅ | **`session.cookie_httponly = true`** | JavaScript cannot read the session cookie (mitigates XSS). |
| ✅ | **`session.cookie_samesite = Strict`** (or `Lax`) | Stops most CSRF attempts even without a hidden token. |
| ✅ | **`password_hash()` / `password_verify()`** | Modern, adaptive hashing (bcrypt, Argon2, etc.). |
| ✅ | **Prepared statements everywhere** | No SQL injection. |
| ✅ | **Rate‑limit login attempts** (e.g., via MySQL `failed_attempts` column, Redis, or a simple `sleep(1)` after a failed login). |
| ✅ | **Input validation & sanitisation** (filter email, limit string lengths). |
| ✅ | **Regenerate session ID after login** (`session_regenerate_id(true)`). |
| ✅ | **Never store plain passwords or reusable tokens**. |
| ✅ | **Hide detailed error messages from users** (log them server‑side instead). |
| ✅ | **Set proper file permissions** (e.g., `chmod 640 config.php`). |
| ✅ | **Consider CSRF tokens + SameSite cookies**. |
| ✅ | **Optional: Email verification** (send a one‑time link before activating account). |
| ✅ | **Optional: Password reset flow** (token stored hashed, limited lifetime). |

