### Bonus : Utiliser PHPMailer pour l’envoi SMTP

Si votre serveur ne supporte pas `mail()` ou que vous avez besoin d’authentification SMTP, remplacez la partie **envoi mail** par :

```php
use PHPMailer\PHPMailer\PHPMailer;
use PHPMailer\PHPMailer\SMTP;
require 'vendor/autoload.php';

$mail = new PHPMailer(true);
$mail->isSMTP();
$mail->Host = 'smtp.example.com';
$mail->SMTPAuth = true;
$mail->Username = 'smtp_user';
$mail->Password = 'smtp_pass';
$mail->SMTPSecure = PHPMailer::ENCRYPTION_STARTTLS;
$mail->Port = 587;

$mail->setFrom('backup@example.com', 'Backup MySQL');
$mail->addAddress('admin@example.com');

$mail->Subject = $mailSubject;
$mail->Body    = "Backup joint.";
$mail->addAttachment($fullPath);

$mail->send();
```

Installez PHPMailer via Composer :

```bash
composer require phpmailer/phpmailer
```

